  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.find_maximal_independent_sets -\n    EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.find_maximal_independent_sets.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.find_maximal_independent_sets()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find multiple distinct maximal independent sets.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.find_maximal_independent_sets()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find multiple distinct maximal independent sets.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.find_maximal_independent_sets()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find multiple distinct maximal independent sets.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind multiple distinct maximal independent sets.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L88469-L88578){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.find_maximal_independent_sets(\n    count=10,\n    seed=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Find maximal independent sets](../assets/graphs/find-maximal-independent-sets.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: a five-node graph, a triangle 2, 3, 5 with pendant nodes 1 and 4. Right: three miniature copies, each highlighting one maximal independent set in the accent color, listed beside it: [1, 3], [1, 4, 5], and [2, 4].\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nRuns the randomized `maximal_independent_set()` algorithm repeatedly, each time with a\ndifferent random node order, and keeps every result that hasn't been seen before. A graph\nusually has many maximal independent sets of different sizes, and a single call returns\njust one of them; sampling several lets you explore the alternatives.\n\nThis is useful for:\n\n- approximating a *maximum* independent set by keeping the largest of many candidates\n- finding alternative conflict-free batches (for example, different sets of jobs that\n  can run together) and choosing among them by some other criterion\n- ensemble methods or robustness checks that need several distinct solutions\n\nAt most `3 * count` attempts are made. Duplicate sets are discarded, so the method stops\nearly once `count` distinct sets are found and returns fewer than `count` sets if the\nattempts run out first (for example, when the graph only has a few maximal independent\nsets). Like `maximal_independent_set()`, it ignores edge direction.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[count]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[10]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Number of distinct maximal independent sets to return. Default is `10`. Fewer sets\n    are returned if not enough distinct ones turn up within `3 * count` attempts.\n\n<code>[seed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Base random seed for reproducibility. When given, attempt `i` (counting from `0`)\n    uses seed `seed + i`, so the same `seed=` always returns the same list of sets. If\n    `None` (the default), every attempt draws its order from system entropy and results\n    vary between calls.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   List of distinct maximal independent sets, in the order they were found. Each set is\n    a list of node IDs sorted in ascending order. May contain fewer than `count` sets.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nRuns `maximal_independent_set()` up to $3 \\cdot \\text{count}$ times with distinct\nseeds derived from a common base, giving $O(\\text{count} \\cdot (V + E))$ total work.\nDuplicate results are dropped, so the returned list may be shorter than `count` when\nthe graph's independent structure is tight enough that different starting orders\nkeep converging to the same set. Sampling a diverse pool this way is the usual\nbridge between the fast-but-maximal single call and the slow-but-maximum exact\nsolver: keeping the largest set out of several attempts often approaches the true\nmaximum on real-world graphs.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~maximal_independent_set`) \n\n:   Draw a single maximal independent set.\n\n[](`~maximum_independent_set`) \n\n:   Find a large independent set.\n\n[](`~find_cliques`) \n\n:   List the maximal cliques, a related enumeration.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA 6-node cycle has maximal independent sets of two nodes, opposite each other, and of\nthree, every other node:\n\n::: {#a4e75e8c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ncycle = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"E\"), (\"E\", \"F\"),\n     (\"F\", \"A\")]\n)\n\n[\n    [cycle.get_label_from_id(n) for n in found]\n    for found in cycle.find_maximal_independent_sets(count=5, seed=1)\n]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['A', 'D'], ['C', 'F'], ['B', 'E'], ['B', 'D', 'F'], ['A', 'C', 'E']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Slots of every size\n\n`exams()` joins two of the 14 courses at a made-up college when some student takes both,\nso their exams can't share a time slot. Ten maximal independent sets hold from three to\nseven exams. Chemistry, Philosophy and Data Visualization between them conflict with every\nother exam, so no exam can join their slot, though other slots hold more than twice as\nmany:\n\n::: {#8fcf15e0 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nexams = ec.exams()\nfound = exams.find_maximal_independent_sets(count=10, seed=1)\nsmallest = min(found, key=len)\n\n(\n    sorted(len(s) for s in found),\n    [exams.get_label_from_id(n) for n in smallest],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n([3, 4, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 6, 7],\n ['Chemistry', 'Philosophy', 'Data Visualization'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#2905d7fc .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nexams.plot(highlight=smallest, label_by=\"label\", seed=5)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}: